# duo-sdk Project Conventions

## Package Manager
Use **yarn**, not npm. Run scripts with `yarn <script>` (e.g. `yarn test`, `yarn build`).

## Duo Request Signing
All requests use **v5 signing** (`signV5`) unconditionally — no per-path switching.
Duo recommends v5 for all endpoints; an increasing set of endpoints reject v2 entirely.
Do not reintroduce `sign()` (v2) or a `V5_SIGNATURE_PATHS` allowlist.

## Module Structure
Each resource lives in `src/lib/<resource>/` with three files:
- `<resource>.ts` — class extending the Axios instance
- `<resource>.types.ts` — TypeScript interfaces
- `<resource>.spec.ts` — Jest unit tests (mock Axios, not real HTTP)

## Duo API Response Handling
Always check `data.stat === 'FAIL'` after every Axios call and throw with `data.message` + `data.message_detail`.

## Testing
- **Do not use `jest-mock-axios`** — it is incompatible with Jest 30.3+ and has been removed.
- Mock HTTP with a local `mockHttp` stub object using `jest.fn()`. Declare it at the top of the spec file and reset with `jest.clearAllMocks()` in `beforeEach`:
  ```typescript
  const mockHttp = { get: jest.fn(), post: jest.fn(), put: jest.fn(), delete: jest.fn() }
  beforeEach(() => { jest.clearAllMocks(); resource = new Resource(mockHttp as unknown as AxiosInstance) })
  ```
- For `create-http-agent.spec.ts`, mock the axios module with `jest.mock('axios')` and configure `jest.mocked(axios.create).mockReturnValue(mockInstance)` in `beforeEach`.
- Assert both the happy path and the `stat === 'FAIL'` error path for every method.
- Never make real Duo API calls in tests.
